Rules here rather than in sepolicy/vendor/ for one reason: vendor policy cannot
reference types declared in system/sepolicy/private — the build fails with an
unknown type. system_suspend, adbd_prop, system_adbd_prop, privapp_data_file and
the gmscore_app / untrusted_app domains are all private types, so their rules
must live in SYSTEM_EXT_PRIVATE_SEPOLICY_DIRS (BoardConfig.mk).

Vendor domains — pnpmgr, mnld, epdg_wod, mtk_hal_camera and the rest — stay in
sepolicy/vendor/. Check where a type is declared before choosing the file; it is
not cosmetic.
